          "text": "The installed skill's state-change clause directs applying heat/cool by holding the object and using `heat <object> with microwave 1` / `cool <object> with fridge 1`, and explicitly warns against moving the object into the appliance and toggling its door. Where the target was acquired, candidate runs followed this hold-and-apply form. The clearest contrast is the heat-egg pair: the baseline moved egg 1 into microwave 1 and then opened/closed the microwave repeatedly to the 50-step limit without applying heat (failure), whereas the candidate executed `heat egg 1 with microwave 1` while holding and completed in 9 steps (success). The heat-mug baseline likewise moved mug 4 into microwave 1 and door-toggled to the step limit; the candidate applied `heat cup 1 with microwave 1` directly in Q10, and both sides applied `heat apple 1 with microwave 1` directly in the hot-apple pair (candidate 8 steps vs baseline 14). Because the skill was installed as one joint edit, the hold-and-apply behavior is associated with, but not isolated to, the Q9 improvement, and it did not by itself guarantee success (Q10 still failed).",
